		<help>
			<title>SA-315B Lama</title>
			<key>
				<name>{ }</name>
				<desc>shutdown/start turbines</desc>
			</key>

			<key>
				<name>i</name>
				<desc>toggle ignition switch</desc>
			</key>


			<key>
				<name>r</name>
				<desc>Activate rescue Wich Man. ( winch needs to be fitted )</desc>
			</key>
			<key>
				<name>m/M</name>
				<desc>Raise/lower the winch man</desc>
			</key>


			<key>
				<name>R</name>
				<desc>toggle rotor brake</desc>
			</key>


			<key>
				<name>MMB</name>
				<desc>adjust power lever (middle mouse button) while scrolling the ouse up/down</desc>
			</key>

 <line> </line>
 <line> Lighting. All lighting swiches are located on the overhead panel. Default for all lights is  OFF.</line>
 <line>If you are using HDR, then you need to enable the specific HDR panel lights from the SA-315B Menu.</line>
 <line>Using the HDR panel lights while not in HDR will produce very strange results.</line>
<line> </line>
 <line>For Manual Starting, see below. NOTE, using Auto start does not  Animate everything. </line>
 <line>You will still need to manually set the battery switch </line>
 <line></line>
 <line> Internal checks before starting engine.</line>
<line>Seat - Adjust position  (  Middle mouse button  + scrolling the mouse up/down while the mouse is in free look mode)</line>
<line>Tail rotor pedals - check free movement</line>
<line> Cyclic pitch stick - check free travel then lower fully.</line>
<line> Microphones and earphones - Not implemented.</line>
<line>Safety Harness - not implemented </line>
 <line>Doors - Closed if fitted ( click on the doors to open/close them )</line>
 <line>Fuel Flow control lever in  CLOSED position ( lowered fully - White lever next to the collective )</line>
<line> Servo Systen control cock  - Not implementd </line>
<line> Fuel Shut-off control lever lock in forward position ( Red Lever next to the Fuel Flow  lever ) </line>
<line> Circuit Breakers - Engaged  ( Not Implemented ) </line>
<line> Switch Battery + Generator on ( Batt switch On overhead panel ) </line>
<line>Engine selector switch - not implemented </line>
<line> Rotor Brake RELEASED ( red T lever on the right of the main panel ) </line>
<line> Check - Volt + Electric instruments</line>
<line> Ceck warning lights ( warning light test switch is on the Overhead panel )</line>
<line> Check and adjust Altimeter, compass and clock</line>
<line> Set Avionics switch to ON ( overhead panel )</line>
<line>In the event of night flying, check Interior and exterior lighting </line>
<line> Artificial Horizon and directional gyro CAGED - not implemented</line>
<line> </line>
<line>Starting the Engine + Rotor</line>
<line> Switch the booster punp to  ON and wait 20 sec ( Centre  lower panel ). The fuel low pressure warning light goes out  </line>
<line> Set the starting selector switch to  ON  ( Centre lower Panel  below the Booster Punp switch ). The green START light comes on </line>
<line> Inclease Fuel Flow lever to 63% for Idle </line>
<line> Disengage the satring selector switch - engine will rise to idle. </line>
<line> Switch the booster punp to  OFF </line>
<line> Gradually increase the Fuel Flow to 100% for flight. </line>
<line></line>
<line> SAR Menu option - THIS IS JUST A FUN MULTIPLAYER FEATURE !!</line>
			<line> If you crash your chopper, you can use this menu option to call on another AS350</line>
			<line>or any other chopper running the script, to retrieve your broken chopper and you, as an underslung load.</line>


		</help>


